  "details": "On my account webpage, the default view for “Favorite Friends,” “Favorite Avatars,” and “Favorite Worlds” is set to a specific, unintended sorting group.\n\n \n\nExample: I’ve edited my friend list so that “Favorite Friends” is sorted into groups named “Friend 1,” “Friend 2,” and “Friend 3.”\n\nHowever, whenever I open “Favorite Friends” in my browser, the “Friend 2” sorting group is displayed by default 100% of the time.\n\n \n\nI want “Friend 1” to be displayed by default.\n\n \n\nFor “Favorite Avatars” and “Favorite Worlds,” although the edits I’ve made differ, the default view is similarly set to an unintended sorting group.\n\nI would like the intended sorting group to be displayed by default for these as well.\n\n----\n\nIn Help Desk Request ID #753710,\n\n “Morrigan” says, “Please report this individually on the feedback board.”\n\n \n\nTranslated with DeepL.com (free version)",
